  "backstory": "Sible grew up in a quiet gnomish community nestled deep within an ancient forest. From a young age, she felt a profound connection to the natural world, spending hours exploring the woods and observing the creatures that dwelled within. A vision led her to abandon her village and seek guidance from a reclusive druid, who taught her the ways of nature. Sible has since embraced her solitary existence, finding solace and wisdom in the wilderness. However, a growing concern about the encroachment of civilization on the wild lands has stirred her from her seclusion, prompting her to venture out and protect the natural world.",
  "flaws": [
    "Stubborn and resistant to change, she is slow to trust those outside the natural world.",
    "Overly protective of nature, sometimes to the detriment of others."
  ],
  "ideals": [
    "Nature: The natural world is more important than anything, and its delicate balance must be protected. (Neutral)"
  ],
  "bonds": [
    "The ancient forest where I grew up is sacred to me, and I will defend it against any threat."
  ],
  "traits": [
    "Prefers the company of animals to people.",
    "Always willing to lend a helping hand to those in need, especially if it benefits nature."
  ],
